    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on leveraging elite speed and favorable matchups, headlined by our top-tier plays: **Trea Turner** (78.64) and **Kyle Schwarber** (77.46). Both benefit significantly from facing V\u00e1squez, whose 4.75 xERA provides the most exploitable pitching environment on the board. **Trea Turner** is a locked-in core play, utilizing his speed against a weak arm, while **Yordan Alvarez** (74.26) remains an automatic start despite a tougher matchup against Bubba Chandler, as his elite 0.454 xwOBA provides the ceiling necessary to carry our offensive output. **Junior Caminero** (63.30) rounds out our top-tier options, as his dynamic platoon advantage helps him overcome the park-factor suppression against Flaherty.\n\nStrategic lineup construction heavily accounts for our scarcity in stolen bases. While **Caleb Durbin** (55.04) carries a lower score due to his lower-order positioning, he is an essential start; his 90% steal probability against a slow-delivering pitcher makes him a critical weapon for our league-leading SB goal. Conversely, **Christian Yelich** (54.83) presents a nuanced case; while his score is bolstered by a strong platoon advantage, we are closely monitoring the threat of an elite catcher\u2019s pop time (1.86s). Our most difficult bench decision was **Casey Schmitt** (38.76), who was heavily considered but ultimately excluded due to a poor SP matchup against Kyle Harrison (3.41 xERA) and negative platoon markers that kept him well below our efficiency threshold. \n\nThe primary risks for today involve several \"Lineup Pending\" designations that could force mid-day adjustments. **Luke Raley**, **Carson Benge**, and **Christian Yelich** are currently projected based on historical batting order, but any shift into the bottom third of their respective lineups will necessitate a re-evaluation of their utility. Furthermore, **Carson Benge** faces the toughest test of the day against Logan Gilbert (3.22 xERA), whose elite skill level forced a significant 19% deduction to **Carson Benge**'s projected score. We are keeping **Gary Sanchez** on high alert; should any of our primary starters be scratched, his power profile remains the next best alternative, provided the matchup warrants a late-swap.",
